# Tone Curve

The tone curve is a tool for fine-tuning the tonal range of an image. It maps input tones to output tones across highlights, lights, darks, and shadows.

## How It Works

- **Highlights**: Upper right of curve
- **Lights**: Upper middle
- **Darks**: Lower middle
- **Shadows**: Lower left

Creating an S-curve by pulling up highlights and pulling down shadows increases contrast in the image.

Related to [[Post-Processing]] and [[Global vs Local Adjustments]].
